bishop. Our bishop is ideally placed here, targeting the kingside and queenside.} 13.Bxe4 13...Qd7 {And if Black plays the natural ...Qd7, supporting the light-squared bishop... We've got Qh5 once again, double attacking the c5-bishop and mate.} 14.Qh5 14...f5 {Black can try to fight on with ...f5. We'll respond by taking the bishop.} 15.Nxe6 15...Qxe6 {And when Black recaptures... We can simply capture the f5-pawn.} 16.Bxf5 16...Rxf5 {Black's best is to sac the exchange. We'll recapture with our queen.} 17.Qxf5 17...Qxf5 {Keeping the queens on would be quite dangerous for Black, so Black trades.} 18.Rxf5 {And we recapture with our rook. This is a completely winning position. We're up an exchange and pawn.} *

